log10 Craig axiom = log10((k+1)|phi^b|), symbols.  Certificate and fast-labeller columns are symbols.
Reading: the Craig axiom of canonical proof search grows like N^(L*-1) = 2^Theta(|w|^2) here,
the theory's own derivations like |w|^2, the certificate axiom like |w|^2, and the Craig axiom
of the fast parity labeller like |w|^2.  The blow-up belongs to the construction (padding by the
run time of an exhaustive search), not to the observational regularity.
